      "content": "Given the identical core financials, the risk assessment for Profile C would likely be **Medium**, while Profile D would lean toward **Medium-High**. Although the financial data is similar, the \"Maplewood\" designation (Profile C) suggests stability consistent with higher property values, which slightly mitigates risk. Conversely, the \"West End\" designation (Profile D) combined with lower-end indicators might signal higher local economic instability or higher cost-of-living pressures, slightly elevating the perceived risk compared to Profile C.",
